# Aurelia VIP 3D scene STANDARD

Resume: `@aurelia-scene$` / `$ai-movie$`.

## Owner decision (Oct 15 2026)

The **Aurelia VIP 3D demo** design is approved as a **STANDARD** base layout. Use this procedural room geometry to generate AI scenes repeatedly (still frames, clips, and full **15–30 minute AI movies** from a story bible). Process and prompt templates live in `reports/aurelia-scene-standard/`. Reference implementation: `reports/vip-aurelia-demo/` (`aurelia.json`, `scene3d.js`).

**Status:** documentation standard only — **not** an app build, **not** published to GitHub Pages, **not** Functions deploy unless the owner asks. Billing / ledger work is out of scope (see commit `03988f0` and related VIP billing docs — do not touch).

## Locked vs mutable

| Locked (architecture) | Mutable (story / art direction) |
|---|---|
| Room **32 m × 22 m**, walls **6 m**, eye **1.65 m**, mezzanine **+1.2 m** | Wardrobe, era, palette accents within mood |
| Four areas: **A West Booths**, **B Dance Floor**, **C VIP Mezzanine**, **D Bar Lounge** | Anonymous crowd silhouettes (no faces) |
| **Non-bookable:** main bar, VIP bar, DJ booth, dance-floor zone, entrance, coat check, restrooms, stairs, exits | Bottle service, sparklers, confetti props |
| Circulation paths and door positions | DJ silhouette (no real artist likeness) |
| Camera preset *geometry* (overview, area focus, section focus, walk spawn) | Story beats, time-of-night, music mood |
| Brand placement rules (below) | LED wall *content* (ShoutOut silhouettes only) |

**Never** move walls, bars, DJ booth, stairs, or exits for a story beat. If AI output drifts architecture, regenerate with the architecture-drift repair prompt (`AI-MOVIE-PROCESS.md`).

## Capture method

**Modeled / AI-assisted procedural layout** inspired by club gallery photos — **not** photogrammetry, **not** a survey. **No identifiable patrons** in any render (still, video, or LED wall). Crowds = anonymous silhouettes only.

## Camera presets (match `scene3d.js`)

| Preset | Use |
|---|---|
| **Overview** | Position ~(0, 24, 22) world, target (0, 0, 1) — dollhouse read of all four areas |
| **Area focus** | Center on area bounds; VIP mezz uses +1.2 m floor; distance scales with area size × aspect boost |
| **Section focus** | Table/booth framing with sheet offset (mobile bottom sheet vs side panel) |
| **Walk start** | Spawn **x=7 m, z=19.6 m**, eye height **1.65 m**, yaw **0** (facing north), pitch ~**-0.08** |

## Lighting moods

Base rig (club night): hemisphere **#ffe7c2** / ground **#1a1020**, ambient white, directional key, point **chandeliers #ffd28a**. Named moods for AI direction:

- **club night** — default warm VIP interior
- **arrival red-carpet** — brighter entry, accent on entrance path
- **VIP mezzanine champagne** — cooler highlights on mezz, softer floor
- **dance-floor peak** — stronger beams / haze on Area B (mutable VFX only)
- **closing soft** — dimmer chandeliers, longer shadows, no layout change

## Brand chrome

**FloqR**, **FloqMedia**, **ShoutOut** are brand strings — **never translated**. LED wall may show **ShoutOut silhouette boards** (classic board shapes, no patron photos). Do not invent a second production origin; canonical product links follow `cutoffrequirement.mdc` when cutover applies — these docs are repo-local QA / production notes.

## Film pipeline (summary)

1. **Story bible** — logline, characters (silhouettes), beats, runtime target (15–30 min)
2. **SCENE-LOCK keyframes** — stills that obey locked geometry (`SCENE-LOCK.md`)
3. **Image-to-video** — short clips per beat from keyframes
4. **Assembly** — edit to beat sheet; hold on architecture-locked wide shots between story inserts
5. **Audio** — music mood + optional VO; no uncleared identifiable voice clones
6. **QC / architecture-drift fix** — reject or repair any shot that moved bars, DJ, walls, or exits

Full operator steps: `reports/aurelia-scene-standard/AI-MOVIE-PROCESS.md`.

